      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the primary difference between acetoxy and neutral cure silicone sealants?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The primary difference lies in their chemical curing byproduct. Acetoxy silicones release acetic acid (which smells strongly like vinegar) during curing. This byproduct is acidic and can corrode sensitive metals like copper, brass, zinc, and mild steel, and attack concrete masonry. Neutral cure silicones release non-corrosive alcohols (alkoxy cure) or oximes (oxime cure) during crosslinking, making them safe for metals, concrete, natural stone, and sensitive plastics."
