        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Acetoxy silicones crosslink via the fast hydrolysis of acetoxysilane groups. The acetic acid byproduct itself acts as a mild autocatalyst for the condensation reaction. Alkoxy-based neutral cure silicones undergo a slower thermodynamic hydrolysis of their alkoxy groups, requiring specialized organotitanate or tin catalysts to drive the reaction, which results in a longer skin-over time and a slower deep cure rate."
      }
    },
