      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What makes a silicone sealant food-grade and FDA compliant?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A food-grade silicone sealant is formulated using high-purity polydimethylsiloxane polymers, inert silica fillers, and non-toxic crosslinkers that comply strictly with FDA regulation 21 CFR 177.2600. It must not contain toxic heavy metals (like organotin catalysts above safety limits), phthalate plasticizers, or migratory organic solvents. Additionally, it must be formulated to resist hot water washdowns, oils, and sanitizing chemicals without leaching compounds into contact food."
      }
